<ContentPage title="About" description="Academic background and research interests of Onaïa Savary." image="/spectral/images/banner.jpg" intro="Academic background and research interests.">
			<p class="lead">Onaïa Savary is a PhD student in climatology (PhD started October 2024) at the Centre National de Recherche en Météorologie (CNRM / Météo‑France). Her PhD investigates links between large‑scale atmospheric circulation and precipitation deficits (droughts) in Europe, and the influence of climate change on this relationship.</p>

			<h2>Academic background</h2>
			<p>PhD in Climatology — CNRM / Météo‑France (October 2024 – present). Master 2 in Civil Engineering, preparatory track for the Agrégation — École Normale Supérieure, Paris‑Saclay (September 2021 – July 2023). Classe préparatoire at Lycée (Toulouse). Baccalauréat Scientifique — Lycée Louis Rascol, Albi.</p>

			<h2>Research interests</h2>
			<p>Research topics documented in the CV include drought predictability, weather regimes, atmospheric circulation and the impacts of climate change on drought dynamics.</p>

			<h2>Teaching activities</h2>
			<p>Teaching activities are listed in the CV (private tutoring and presentations at secondary schools); full details are available in the downloadable CV.</p>

